message.content:
Use the CSS `:hover` pseudo-class on the `span`. The basic pattern is:

```html
<span class="hoverable">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.hoverable {
  color: black;
}

.hoverable:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

The `:hover` selector applies styles when the mouse pointer is over the element, and it works on `span` elements as well as links.[5][6]

If you want to change the **background** instead of the text color, use `background-color`:

```css
.hoverable:hover {
  background-color: yellow;
}
```

If your `span` already has an inline `style` attribute, that may override your CSS; in that case, remove the inline styling or use a stronger selector.[1]

